# Line-ending policy for the dual-agent contract registry.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in the system gitconfig, so without this rule Git
# rewrites AGENT_HANDSHAKE.md to CRLF the next time it touches the file. Both
# Claude and Antigravity edit that file on Windows, and a whole-file
# line-ending diff would bury the one or two bullets that actually changed,
# defeating the zero-regression review the registry exists to support.
#
# Deliberately narrow in scope. Do NOT add a repo-wide `* text=auto` rule
# while the working tree carries uncommitted work: that renormalizes every
# tracked file at once and produces exactly the unreadable diff this prevents.
AGENT_HANDSHAKE.md text eol=lf
